{"duration_api_ms":26530,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b0f436ff-795c-463e-b9ad-e7fc5a791e8b","total_cost_usd":0.1677286,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16995,"cache_read_input_tokens":171568,"output_tokens":2420,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":583},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":16995},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":626,"cache_read_input_tokens":39646,"cache_creation_input_tokens":899,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":899,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":2420,"cacheReadInputTokens":171568,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16995,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1677286,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":583,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":6,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Recovery now treats a panic with `http.ErrAbortHandler` (Go's built-in signal for deliberately aborting a request) the same way it treats a broken pipe. It logs one short line with no stack trace, records the error on the context and aborts without writing a 500.\n\n- **Changes:** 5 lines in `recovery.go` set the existing `brokenPipe` flag when the panic value is an error matching `http.ErrAbortHandler` (wrapped errors also match). `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` in `recovery_test.go` checks that the response keeps the status the handler set, and that the log contains the error message but no `panic recovered` stack trace.\n- **Why this approach:** reusing the broken-pipe path keeps it to a 5-line diff. The other option was to re-panic so Go's HTTP server would handle it. That bypasses gin's recovery entirely and is a bigger change in behaviour.\n- **Tests:** the new test failed before the fix (500 status plus a full stack trace) and passes after. It fails again when only `recovery.go` is reverted. `go test -count=1 ./...` passes in every package, and `go vet` and `gofmt -l` are clean.\n- **Behaviour change to be aware of:** a custom handler passed to `CustomRecovery` is no longer called for `http.ErrAbortHandler`, the same as for broken pipes already.\n- **Not done:** I couldn't run golangci-lint because it isn't installed here. Nothing is committed.","ttft_ms":2564,"type":"result","duration_ms":33743,"uuid":"04d53858-9636-4e47-a970-351a8f91990e","ttft_stream_ms":2164,"time_to_request_ms":125,"first_content_frame_ms":2164,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
